{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48228", "qid": "gen-rwfaithful-4e59b411", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses report a measurement of f_a3^ggH (Hgg CP-odd effective fractional cross section)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph contains several results that measure observables related to the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel. Here are the relevant analyses:\n\n1. **$CP$ Properties of Higgs Boson Interactions with Top Quarks in the $t\\bar{t}H$ and $tH$ Processes Using $H\\rightarrow\\gamma\\gamma$ with the ATLAS Detector**\n   - This analysis measures observables related to the CP properties of Higgs boson interactions with top quarks, including the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n2. **Combination and interpretation of differential Higgs boson production cross sections in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**\n   - This analysis combines and interprets differential Higgs boson production cross sections, which may include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n3. **Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}$**\n   - This analysis combines searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production, which could involve measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n4. **Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using $H\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}$ decays in the ATLAS detector**\n   - This analysis constrains Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum, which might include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n5. **Evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons**\n   - This analysis provides evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons, which might indirectly involve measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n6. **HH->WWgamgam analysis result**\n   - This analysis focuses on the HH->WWgamgam decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n7. **HH->bb gamgam analysis result**\n   - This analysis focuses on the HH->bb gamgam decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n8. **HH->bb tautau analysis result**\n   - This analysis focuses on the HH->bb tautau decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n9. **HH->bbWW, WW->4q all-hadronic analysis result**\n   - This analysis focuses on the HH->bbWW, WW->4q all-hadronic decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n10. **HH->bbWW, WW->lvqq/2l2nu analysis result**\n    - This analysis focuses on the HH->bbWW, WW->lvqq/2l2nu decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n11. **HH->bbZZ(4l) analysis result**\n    - This analysis focuses on the HH->bbZZ(4l) decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n12. **HH->gamgamtautau analysis result**\n    - This analysis focuses on the HH->gamgamtautau decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\n13. **HH->multilepton analysis result**\n    - This analysis focuses on the HH->multilepton decay, which could include measurements of the CP-odd effective fractional cross section in the Hgg channel.\n\nTo provide a more precise answer,", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06